WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.480
Our case now identifies a long high-current low-voltage segment as the limiting

2
00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.000
part of the proposed power path.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.320
A sidecar or a higher-voltage feed with conversion nearer the load may

4
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.260
address that segment.

5
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:15.880
The team must compare supported implementations rather than treating either concept as

6
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:16.860
a complete solution.

7
00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:20.240
Mark which segment changes and recalculate the constraints there.

8
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.120
Then review the remaining lower-voltage path.

9
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:27.000
If its connection or busbar limit still blocks the workload, the proposal

10
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.480
hasn't solved the whole problem.

11
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.980
Add the changed protection, thermal, service and site boundaries to the evidence

12
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:33.300
record.

13
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.980
Pause and state the next decision in one sentence: which architecture is

14
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.200
being considered, which constraint it addresses, and which evidence remains necessary?

15
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.060
A useful answer doesn't need a universal winner.

16
00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:49.200
It needs a configuration-specific reason to proceed with a bounded review or

17
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.740
test, followed by clear acceptance conditions before operation.

